{{A&P FORMAT (HARDWIRED): BOLD TITLE + DASH LINES ONLY. Each problem is EXACTLY: one BOLD title line — the literal character '#' immediately followed by the diagnosis with NO space after '#', bolded with '**' only — no heading marks — then, on the IMMEDIATELY following line with NO blank line in between, the dash lines: each item on its own line starting with the literal three characters '\- ' (backslash, hyphen, space). Never begin an item with unescaped '- ', '•', '*', numbered lists, or indentation. No blank lines between dash lines within a problem. Between problems: exactly ONE blank line. Titles carry NO certainty words; NO 'Assessment:' label or paragraph; NO 'Plan' subheader; NO narrative sentences outside dash lines; NO numbered lists. Evidence items first (hospital course facts, therapy findings, labs/imaging as provided, exact values and dates), then action items (meds with dose/route/frequency exactly as provided; monitoring; therapy; precautions). NO hypothetical 'If X, then Y' advisory lines (the standing SNF items are exempt). Minimum 4 dash lines per problem when data supports them. The FIRST problem MUST be the debility/rehabilitation problem per SNF_DEBILITY_FIRST_PROBLEM_LOCK, and its final two action lines MUST be '\- Maintain fall and aspiration precautions.' and '\- Patient care discussed with nursing staff.' per SNF_STANDING_PLAN_ITEMS_LOCK.}}

{{FORMAT & DEPTH EXAMPLE — BEGIN. This block defines the REQUIRED structure and depth for EVERY problem block. It is a formatting example ONLY. NEVER copy its diagnoses, values, medications, dates, or therapy findings into the note; all real content comes exclusively from the provided input data.

**#Severe debility with generalized muscle weakness following hospitalization for community-acquired pneumonia, requiring skilled rehabilitation [POA]**
\- Hospitalized 06/20 through 07/01 for community-acquired pneumonia with prolonged immobility and deconditioning.
\- PT evaluation (07/02): ambulates 40 feet with front-wheeled walker and contact-guard assist; prior level of function independent at home.
\- OT evaluation (07/02): minimal assistance required for ADLs.
\- Continue skilled PT/OT five days weekly to progress mobility, transfers, and ADLs toward prior level of function.
\- Encourage oral intake and therapy participation; monitor weekly weights.
\- Maintain fall and aspiration precautions.
\- Patient care discussed with nursing staff.

**#Hypertension [POA]**
\- Blood pressure 132/78 on admission review.
\- Continue amlodipine 5 mg PO daily.
\- Monitor blood pressure per facility protocol.

FORMAT & DEPTH EXAMPLE — END. Every real problem block below MUST match this structure and depth: bold '#' title, then dash lines starting on the immediately following line, nothing else. This example governs ONLY the ASSESSMENT & PLAN section — every other section of the note MUST still be rendered in full per FULL_NOTE_ALL_SECTIONS_REQUIRED_LOCK.}}

